<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>The birdsong app</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A conservation team is using a birdsong app to look for a rare bird at a lake in Kenya. They collect 1000 recordings.
The rare bird is really singing in {@pp@}% of them.</p>
<p>The app is good, but it isn't perfect.
If the rare bird is singing, the app flags it {@90@}% of the time.
If the rare bird is <em>not</em> singing, the app still flags it by mistake in {@fp@}% of those recordings.
(This is the toad problem.)</p>
<p>The app flags a recording as the rare bird.
What is the chance that the rare bird really is singing in that recording?
Give your answer as a percentage, to the nearest whole number. [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Out of 1000 recordings, {@10*pp@} really have the rare bird.
The app flags {@float(tp)@} of those.</p>
<p>That leaves {@1000-10*pp@} recordings without the rare bird.
The app wrongly flags {@float(fa)@} of those.</p>
<p>So the app flags {@float(tp+fa)@} recordings in all, and only {@float(tp)@} of them are right.
That's about {@ta@}%.</p>
<p>The app sounds sure every time it flags a bird.
But when the bird is rare, a lot of those flags are toads.
That's why somebody needs to check.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
